title: [+ chancellor +] is Sacked!
view-if: chancellor_party == "Royalist" and rubicon_mini and president != "DuFour" and president != "Gallax" and president != "Gorrick" and president != "Frask"
new-page: true
tags: event
max-visits: 1

= [+ chancellor +] is Sacked

The newly elected president, [+ president +], holds little sympathy for [+ chancellor +] or his party, and has compelled his resignation as Chancellor. The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>, however, refuses to yield—denouncing the move as “anti-democratic,” insisting that [+ chancellor +] is still the head of government, and openly threatening armed resistance.

What are we to do now?

- @fight: We will fight on the streets to prevent Gallax from retaining power.
- @give_up: We will vote against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> in the Assembly.

@fight

Do we realize that this means civil war, against the full force of the state?

- @civil_war: Yes.
- @give_up: We are not ready for war. Instead, we will vote against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> in the Assembly.

@give_up
go-to: give_up_1 if president_ideology != "Left" or army_loyalty > 0.2; give_up_2 if (president_ideology == "Left" and army_loyalty <= 0.2)

The President is on our side, but the Commonwealth Army remains divided.

@give_up_1
on-arrival: {!
Q.next_election_month = Q.month + 3;
Q.next_election_time = Q.time + 3;
if (Q.next_election_month > 12) {
    Q.next_election_month -= 12;
    Q.next_election_year = Q.year + 1;
} else {
    Q.next_election_year = Q.year;
}

Q.pro_republic += 15;

Q.commons_royalist -= 6;
Q.disfavored_royalist -= 6;
Q.commons_collectivist += 3;
Q.disfavored_collectivist += 3;
Q.commons_marcher += 3;
Q.disfavored_marcher += 3;

Q.loyalist_strength *= 0.8;

Q.old_chancellor = Q.chancellor;

Q.chancellor = "Askew";
Q.chancellor_party = "Unionist";

Q.foreign_minister_party = "Gold";
if (Q.lvp_formed) Q.foreign_minister_party = "LVP";
Q.interior_minister_party = "Unionist";
Q.justice_minister_party = "I";
Q.labor_minister_party = "Unionist";
Q.army_minister_party = "I";
Q.economic_minister_party = Q.ddp_name;
if (Q.lvp_formed) Q.economic_minister_party = "LVP";
Q.finance_minister_party = "Gold";
if (Q.lvp_formed) Q.finance_minister_party = "LVP";
Q.agriculture_minister_party = "Unionist";

if (Q.president_ideology == "Left") {
    Q.chancellor = "Vesh"; 
    Q.chancellor_party = "Marcher";
    Q.marcher_caretaker = 1;
    Q.foreign_minister_party = "I"; 
    Q.interior_minister_party = "I"; 
    Q.justice_minister_party = "I"; 
    Q.labor_minister_party = "I"; 
    Q.army_minister_party = "I"; 
    Q.economic_minister_party = "I"; 
    Q.finance_minister_party = "I"; 
    Q.agriculture_minister_party = "I";
}

Q.gold_left += 4;
Q.ddp_left += 2;
Q.lvp_left += 4;
Q.bourgeois_cooperation += 3;
Q.liberal_cooperation += 5;

Q.rubicon_mini = 0;
Q.rubicon_mini_leave = 1;
!}

Still, they place more trust in [+ president +] than in Chancellor [+ old_chancellor +], and under this influence, [+ old_chancellor +] was forced to accept his defeat. His removal, along with the replacement of many <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> cabinet ministers, has stopped the Commonwealth's slippery slope into dictatorship.

[? if chancellor == "Askew": Edmund Askew of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is appointed as interim chancellor. ?][? if chancellor == "Vesh": Joran Vesh of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> is selected as appointed chancellor. ?]

The next elections are set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year + 2365 +].

@give_up_2

Unfortunately, the President’s left-wing leanings make him an unacceptable figure to the <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> strongholds of the state. The Commonwealth Army refuses to take his side over that of [+ chancellor +]. Despite holding the highest office in the land, the President finds himself powerless, outmaneuvered by [+ chancellor +].

Eventually, he is ousted through legally questionable means, and new elections are held under the watchful eye of <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> troopers—securing Gallax’s rise to absolute power.

the Commonwealth is lost.

- @game_over: Game over.